   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT transferring certain state property located in the town of Queensbury\nto the county of Warren",
    "basePrintNo": "S8588",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8588-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Warren County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8588\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act transferring certain state property located in the town of\nQueensbury to the county of Warren\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo transfer surplus property from the state Division of Military and\nNaval Affairs to Warren County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Permits the transfer of property in the town of Queensbury\nfrom the state to Warren County, pending consent and approval of the\nDivision of Military and Naval Affairs.\n\nSection 2 - Provides the metes and bounds of the property that would be\ntransferred. Section 3 - Provides effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn May 2025, the Warren County Board of Supervisors passed a resolution\nfor this transfer.  County officials believe the surplus property,\nlocated on Fox Farm Road in Queensbury, could provide necessary storage\nfor the county Sheriff's Office.  In discussions, DMNA officials have\nbeen supportive of this proposal.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
