    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Warren County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8588A\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act transferring certain state property located in the town of\nQueensbury to the county of Warren\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo transfer surplus property from the state Division of Military and\nNaval Affairs to Warren County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- Permits the transfer of property in the town of Queensbury\nfrom the state to Warren County, pending consent and approval of the\nDivision of Military and Naval Affairs.\n\nSection 2 - Provides the metes and bounds of the property that would be\ntransferred. Section 3 - Provides that the county may a survey to the\ncommissioner of OGS\n\nSection 4 - Provides for the land conveyance if the county applies for\nthe tranfser within one year of the effective date.\n\nSection 5 - Establishes conditions for allowable uses and other limita-\ntions.\n\nSection 6 - Requires to county to enter into an agreement with the state\nfor the continued use of pre-existing radio equipment.\n\nSection 7 - Provides effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn May 2025, the Warren County Board of Supervisors passed a resolution\nfor this transfer.\n\nCounty officials believe the surplus property, located on Fox Farm Road\nin Queensbury, could provide necessary storage for the county Sheriff's\nOffice.\n\nIn discussions, DMNA officials have been supportive of this proposal.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DA I E:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n\n\n",
